==Russian==

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|ru|cu|врачь}}, from {{der|ru|sla-pro|*vьračь}}. Synchronically equivalent to {{affix|ru|врать|-ач|id2=agent noun}}. Originally meant "witch-doctor, enchanter".

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA}}
* {{audio|ru|Ru-{{PAGENAME}}.ogg|Audio}}
* {{rhymes|ru|at͡ɕ|s=1}}

===Noun===
{{ru-noun+|b|a=an|}}

# {{lb|ru|medicine|formal}} [[therapist]], not [[surgeon]], not [[hospital]] [[nurse]]
# [[doc]], [[vet]], [[medic]], [[physician]], [[doctor]]

====Usage notes====
# A female medical doctor is referred to as {{m|ru|врач}}, or {{m|ru|[[же́нщина]]-врач}}, or, colloquially only, {{m|ru|врачи́ха}}, which is dispreferred.
# The archaic vocative form {{m|ru|вра́чу}} is currently found only in the set phrase:
#: {{uxi|ru|'''вра́чу''', исцели́ся сам|physician, heal thyself}}

====Declension====
{{ru-noun-table|b|a=an|voc=вра́чу}}

